From a83cd3a3d693801bd66f82e6d0c63656d4be2dcf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mesh-LLM CI <ci@mesh-llm.local>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 10:32:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] deepseek41: note the engram gate-weight reshape as static

The stage program install for any range containing an engram layer failed with:

    stage program reshape requires an explicit non-singleton geometry recipe:
    blk.1.engram_k.weight (reshaped) dims=256x1x1x1 source_dims=64x4x1x1
    source_dynamic_axis=-1

The reshape in question is not a token-relative one. It is the gate weights being flattened to
broadcast over the hc copies, ggml_reshape_2d(w, hc_dim, 1), and it owns no dynamic axis at all. At
n_tokens == 1 its destination (hc_dim, 1, 1, 1) has several axes equal to the token count, so the
extractor cannot rule out a token-relative reading and rejects the program. Recording the static
geometry removes the ambiguity; deepseek4.cpp annotates its views the same way.

Found with tools/v41-mktiny.cpp, a synthetic tiny deepseek41 model that reproduces this failure
exactly (64x4 -> 256 there, 5120x4 -> 20480 on the real model) in seconds. The next failure is
further along: the engram request input has no stage-program input kind, which needs the same
treatment qwen4exp_ple got.
---
 src/models/deepseek41.cpp | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/models/deepseek41.cpp b/src/models/deepseek41.cpp
index d8539b5..66c76e9 100644
--- a/src/models/deepseek41.cpp
+++ b/src/models/deepseek41.cpp
@@ -428,7 +428,13 @@ ggml_tensor * llama_model_deepseek41::graph::build_engram(
         t = ggml_rms_norm(ctx0, t, norm_rms_eps);
         t = ggml_reshape_2d(ctx0, t, hc_dim, nt);
         dsv4_note_source_dimension(t, 1, 0, 2);
-        t = ggml_mul(ctx0, t, ggml_reshape_2d(ctx0, w, hc_dim, 1));
+        // The gate weights are reshaped only to broadcast over the copies. That reshape owns no
+        // dynamic axis, and at n_tokens == 1 its destination (hc_dim, 1, 1, 1) has several axes equal
+        // to the token count, so without an explicit static note the planner cannot rule out a
+        // token-relative reading and rejects the whole stage program.
+        ggml_tensor * gate = ggml_reshape_2d(ctx0, w, hc_dim, 1);
+        skippy_stage_geometry_note(gate, skippy_stage_geometry_static(gate));
+        t = ggml_mul(ctx0, t, gate);
         t = ggml_reshape_3d(ctx0, t, n_embd, hc, nt);
         dsv4_note_source_dimension(t, 2, 0, 1);
         return t;
-- 
